  "id": "Compound::DB00705 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Delavirdine is linked to Cyp1a2 through a series of molecular interactions that span multiple biological pathways. The evidence suggests that Delavirdine, as a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is part of a broader class of compounds that includes Rilpivirine, which binds directly to Cyp1a2. This connection is reinforced by the shared lowest common ancestor with Rilpivirine, both belonging to the Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound class and the Non-Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitor category. The pathway also highlights a potential metabolic interaction, as Delavirdine is directly associated with Cyp2c9, which in turn participates in oxidoreductive activity involving quinones. This suggests a possible metabolic pathway where Delavirdine may influence Cyp1a2 through the intermediary of Cyp2c9, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of drug-target interactions, emphasizing the role of metabolic enzymes in drug metabolism and the importance of considering multiple layers of molecular relationships in understanding drug action.",
